+\subsection{P2 evolving-profile energy assessment (not a law revision)}
+Direct phase irreversibility is verified for the selected fixed-mesh fixture.
+All constitutive and coupling choices above remain unchanged. Consistent surface
+normalization at $0.025$ m still has $0.8569$--$0.9698\%$ maximum source spatial
+error on retained strongly damaged fields, above the provisional $0.5\%$ target.
+Native zero-input particle stress histories have exact Maxwell partitioning;
+FE representation error remains separate from repeated-transfer drift.
+
+On matched Stokes quadrature and exact native-step Maxwell time integration,
+profile work $W_C$ balances bulk storage and dissipation; it need not vanish.
+The elastic-limit kinematics at fixed displacement, committed viscous internal
+variables and elastic cohesive slip gives
+\[
+ \delta E_b=-\sum_a JxW_a\frac{Z_a}{G}(\boldsymbol\tau_a:\boldsymbol S_a)
+                  \delta\chi_a,\qquad
+ \delta\chi=\delta h/I_h-h\,\delta I_h/I_h^2.
+\]
+This is an additional variation beyond the selected reduced fault energy.
+A total-energy phase formulation would have to derive its treatment together
+with the normalization projection adjoint and peak-history dissipation. It is
+not implemented here and shall not be added to H as a compensating increment.
+The present assessment leaves the governing choices intact and records total
+profile-energy closure as unresolved. See
+\texttt{propagation/P2\_accuracy\_energy\_derivation.md} and its report.
+The conditional finer coupled comparison and P3 remain deferred.
 
